# R6I one-child native entry R2 — unsigned preparation

This is a new, private R6I execution candidate. It is source preparation only.
No Main review/admission/once record was created, the R6I empty approval was not
written, and SSH/native/COMSOL/JVM/GUI were not run.

The remote payload is based on the exact Main-reviewed R6I gate, helper, inner
binding, PREBIRTH binding, R14 binding, and embedded R6B lease. Before dispatch,
it checks the captured empty `MAIN_APPROVAL` raw proof and gate projection, then
opens the existing file once and compares the legacy volume/file-index/size
domain separately from the native six-field fingerprint. It uses the frozen
R6B `R14AuthorityRootOpsR6B._write_flush_readback` implementation on that same
handle for an empty readback followed by one exact approval write, flush, and
readback. It rechecks object identity, creation time, link count, owner SID and
descriptor before the unchanged R6I gate is invoked. The result retains all
six native fingerprint fields from before and after the write, including the
observed change and write times. A failed or ambiguous write cannot trigger a
second write or gate invocation.

The regression controls exercise the actual R2 `_same_handle_write` consumer
and the exact R6B writer method. A synthetic in-memory Win32/API shim supplies
the platform boundary; it does not claim a Windows runtime result. Positive
coverage verifies same-handle write/readback, unchanged security, and exact
approval bytes. Negative controls reject changed legacy identity, any changed
native identity/time field, owner or descriptor drift before write, and
post-write descriptor drift. There are also controls for captured-proof
projection, exact approval rendering, gate `SystemExit` diagnostics, and
strict-SSH check-only behavior.

`templates/` contains only explicitly unsigned templates. The R6I approval
template is copied byte-for-byte from the accepted R1 schema so the frozen gate
continues to enforce its exact closed field set; its `UNSIGNED_TEMPLATE_NOT_AUTHORITY`
status and `NOT_ISSUED` nonce are not executable approval values. The separate
R2 source-review record pins both the current live RESUME snapshot and the
historical R6I PREP checkpoint. Those hashes have different meanings and must
not be substituted for the frozen gate's `current_resume_sha256` field, which
is validated against the PREBIRTH binding.

The exact outer route remains `ssh -T` with batch mode, strict host-key
checking, no connection sharing, and one stdin payload followed by EOF to one
original Popen. The remote interpreter uses `-I -B -` (not `-S`, which would
hide the reviewed installed `mcp` dependency). Remote scope is one native child
for at most 60 seconds, with COMSOL/JVM/GUI/Study/solver all zero. The local
wrapper retains and passively waits on that same SSH Popen until natural
terminal; it has no retry, replay, signal, or kill path.

The live RESUME hash recorded by the last check-only run is a review-time
snapshot. If RESUME changes before Main admission, the source review/admission
must bind the new snapshot; the historical PREP checkpoint remains separately
bound. The wrapper's fixed run root is fresh and absent at preparation time.

See `evidence/CROSS_PACKET_W23_R16_R15_PROVENANCE_NOTE_R1.json` for a separate
read-only reconciliation of stale R15-labeled provenance fields in the W23 R16
packet. No W23 packet file was modified, and R6I R2 consumes no W23 source.
